From b91422117f9158b20c849438a5b8476f7694c2ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cosmin Tanislav <demonsingur@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:41:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 04/23] dt-bindings: media: i2c: max96717: add support for
 MAX9295A
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260930-gmsl2-3_serdes-v18-0-43117818f499@analog.com]

MAX9295A is an older variant of the MAX96717 which does not support
tunnel mode.

Document the compatibility.

Signed-off-by: Cosmin Tanislav <demonsingur@gmail.com>
Acked-by: Rob Herring (Arm) <robh@kernel.org>
Tested-by: Martin Hecht <mhecht73@gmail.com>
Tested-by: Tomi Valkeinen <tomi.valkeinen@ideasonboard.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/maxim,max96717.yaml      | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/maxim,max96717.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/maxim,max96717.yaml
index d73a980..2159fd8 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/maxim,max96717.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/maxim,max96717.yaml
@@ -24,12 +24,17 @@ description:
 
   The GMSL2 serial link operates at a fixed rate of 3Gbps or 6Gbps in the
   forward direction and 187.5Mbps in the reverse direction.
+
   MAX96717F only supports a fixed rate of 3Gbps in the forward direction.
 
+  MAX9295A only supports pixel mode.
+
 properties:
   compatible:
     oneOf:
-      - const: maxim,max96717f
+      - enum:
+          - maxim,max9295a
+          - maxim,max96717f
       - items:
           - enum:
               - maxim,max96717
